p.src:
The mass relation displays the identification: $M_{D0}(n)=\frac{n}{g_s\ell_s}
=\frac{n}{R_{11}}
=M_{\mathrm{KK}}(n).$  (Editorial clarification: Susskind calls the D0-branes the gravitons of the eleven-dimensional theory. More precisely, their bound states are the Kaluza–Klein momentum modes of the eleven-dimensional supergravity multiplet, whose massless sector contains the graviton. The distinction preserves the lecture’s physical identification while avoiding a literal one-particle overstatement.)

